      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FARNACE (8) has the right recent form to break through after running second at Murray Bridge, beaten a length by Czech Out, and that followed a BM64 run at Morphettville which reads well for a Maiden of this standard. She has placed three times at around 1050m and expected to be in the finish. LETHAL HARRY (6) is the key fresh element, having won a Morphettville Parks trial and coming from a stable with a sound debut record, while his family has already produced early performers over similar trips. Watch for any market moves. SCOOPED (4) resumes off a two-month freshen after tackling Saturday company on heavy ground and was close up in Class 2 grade two starts back, so his best form is clearly competitive. Worth consideration. VIA NICCOLINA (7) went close at this track last start and has placed twice around this trip, leaving her as a genuine chance if she repeats that latest effort.",
